1
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:11,426
Why can we freely post Chopin on YouTube, but not "Tombe la neige"?

2
00:00:11,556 --> 00:00:17,422
Because copyright lasts 70 years even after the author dies.

3
00:00:17,552 --> 00:00:24,594
Today, let's explore copyright around the world and how it is passed on to family.

4
00:00:27,124 --> 00:00:34,622
Copyright is born automatically the moment you create a song, book, painting or photo.

5
00:00:34,752 --> 00:00:39,082
You don't need to register it.

6
00:00:39,212 --> 00:00:47,214
After a set period, it becomes everyone's: the public domain.

7
00:00:49,744 --> 00:00:53,402
That period differs by country.

8
00:00:53,532 --> 00:00:59,950
Since 2013, Korea protects works for 70 years after the author's death.

9
00:01:00,080 --> 00:01:05,970
The US, Japan and France also protect for 70 years after death.

10
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:09,806
China protects for 50 years after death.

11
00:01:09,936 --> 00:01:20,074
The US has a different rule for older works: as of 2026, works published in 1930 or earlier are free to use.

12
00:01:22,604 --> 00:01:27,486
The count starts on January 1 of the year after the author's death.

13
00:01:27,616 --> 00:01:34,706
Chopin died in 1849, so his music became everyone's long ago.

14
00:01:34,836 --> 00:01:45,646
In Korea, painter Lee Jung-seop (d. 1956) is public domain, but Park Soo-keun (d. 1965) is protected until 2035.

15
00:01:45,776 --> 00:01:49,842
Just nine years made all the difference.

16
00:01:52,372 --> 00:01:56,894
Let's look at popular songs on YouTube.

17
00:01:57,024 --> 00:02:06,322
Beethoven's Für Elise, Pachelbel's Canon, Silent Night and Jingle Bells are all free.

18
00:02:06,452 --> 00:02:13,014
Korea's national anthem is free to use: the composer's family donated the copyright to the nation in 2005.

19
00:02:13,144 --> 00:02:21,602
But White Christmas, Last Christmas and Tombe la neige are still protected.

20
00:02:21,732 --> 00:02:28,318
The Korean song "Spring of My Hometown": the melody is free, but the lyrics are protected until 2051.

21
00:02:28,448 --> 00:02:36,930
Remember: even if a song is free, a famous performer's recording has its own rights.

22
00:02:39,460 --> 00:02:43,046
Paintings and books work the same way.

23
00:02:43,176 --> 00:02:51,970
Van Gogh, da Vinci and Kim Hong-do are public domain, so we can use them freely in this video.

24
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:57,030
Picasso's paintings are protected until 2043.

25
00:02:57,160 --> 00:03:04,490
The Little Prince is free in Korea, but protected in France until 2032.

26
00:03:04,620 --> 00:03:08,926
The same work can be treated differently in each country.

27
00:03:11,456 --> 00:03:16,914
So what happens to copyright when the author dies?

28
00:03:17,044 --> 00:03:21,974
Like a house, it is inherited by the family automatically.

29
00:03:22,104 --> 00:03:29,146
If there are several heirs, they agree on how to divide it; lawyers help with disputes and contracts.

30
00:03:29,276 --> 00:03:36,174
For music, once the heirs register with the copyright society, royalties go to the family.

31
00:03:36,304 --> 00:03:42,242
Tax accountants value the copyright and help file the inheritance tax.

32
00:03:42,372 --> 00:03:48,190
In Korea, inheritance tax must be filed within six months from the end of the month of death.

33
00:03:48,320 --> 00:03:53,970
After that, yearly royalties are subject to income tax.

34
00:03:56,500 --> 00:04:02,150
Korea's inheritance tax rates range from 10% to 50%.

35
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:08,482
Interestingly, inheriting copyright can end up a loss or a gain.

36
00:04:08,612 --> 00:04:17,502
Tax is based on estimated future income; if the song fades, real income is lower, so it's a loss.

37
00:04:17,632 --> 00:04:23,402
But if an old song becomes popular again through a drama or YouTube, it's a gain.

38
00:04:23,532 --> 00:04:32,182
Inheritance tax differs too: up to 55% in Japan, and none in China.

39
00:04:34,712 --> 00:04:40,218
Copyright is an invisible house an author leaves to the family.

40
00:04:40,348 --> 00:04:45,374
And after 70 years, it becomes a gift to the whole world.

41
00:04:45,504 --> 00:04:51,850
For real inheritance and tax matters, please consult a tax accountant or a lawyer.

42
00:04:51,980 --> 00:04:58,254
A free study page with a calculator is linked in the description.

43
00:04:58,384 --> 00:05:03,914
This was Sungsil Piano. Thank you.
